title: SPIR-V Specification
author: John Kessenich, Google
author: Boaz Ouriel, Intel
author: Raun Krisch, Intel
changes:

=== Changes from Version 1.5

- New Functionality:
 * Khronos SPIR-V issue #515: The <<FP_Fast_Math_Mode, *FPFastMathMode*>> decoration may now be used with <<OpFNegate, *OpFNegate*>>,
                              with the binary floating-point comparison instructions
                              (including <<OpOrdered, *OpOrdered*>> and <<OpUnordered, *OpUnordered*>>),
                              and with <<OpExtInst, *OpExtInst*>> where expressly permitted by the extended instruction set.
 * #661: Added a *Nontemporal* <<Image_Operands,Image Operand>>.

- Extensions Incorporated into SPIR-V 1.6:
* SPV_KHR_non_semantic_info, see <<OpExtInstImport, *OpExtInstImport*>>.
* SPV_KHR_integer_dot_product
* SPV_KHR_terminate_invocation
* SPV_EXT_demote_to_helper_invocation, with changes:
  Only <<OpDemoteToHelperInvocation,*OpDemoteToHelperInvocationEXT*>> was incorporated.
  Instead of using *OpIsHelperInvocationEXT*, modules should use *Volatile* loads of
  the *HelperInvocation* <<BuiltIn,built-in variable>>.

- Deprecations and Removals, from Khronos SPIR-V issues:
 * Removed <<OpLessOrGreater, *OpLessOrGreater*>>.  Use <<OpFOrdNotEqual, *OpFOrdNotEqual*>> instead.
 * #620: The *WorkgroupSize* <<BuiltIn,built-in>> is deprecated starting with version 1.6.
 * #645: The _True Label_ and _False Label_ of an <<OpBranchConditional, *OpBranchConditional*>> must not be the same,
         starting with version 1.6.
 * #584: Disallow _Dim_ *Buffer* in <<OpTypeSampledImage, *OpTypeSampledImage*>> and <<OpSampledImage, *OpSampledImage*>>
         starting with version 1.6.
 * Deprecated <<OpKill, *OpKill*>>, in favor of <<OpTerminateInvocation, *OpTerminateInvocation*>>,
   or <<OpDemoteToHelperInvocation, *OpDemoteToHelperInvocation*>>.

- Reserve enumerants for the SPV_KHR_fragment_shader_barycentric extension.
